# Fix: Avatar images cut off at top in "Les Mots" and other games

## Context

In Zoe's portal, family member avatars (maman, papa, félix, zoé, moustache) appear as word illustrations in "Les Mots" and other games. The cartoon portrait images are 512x512px (square) displayed in square containers with `border-radius: 50%` creating a circular crop. Since the images are the same aspect ratio as the container, `object-fit: cover` fills the square exactly — the `object-position` values currently set (e.g. `50% 25%`) have no effect because there's no overflow to position.

The circle naturally clips the corners of the square image. The top of each character's head/hair extends across the full width of the image, so the circular curvature clips it — visible especially at the larger sizes used in games (up to 130px) vs. the home screen (~55-80px).

## Fix

Scale the `<img>` down to ~85% with `transform: scale(0.85)` inside the circular container, and add a background color to fill the exposed gap. This gives ~7.5% more breathing room on each edge, keeping the head/hair fully visible within the circle.

Remove the now-ineffective `object-position` values (they do nothing with matching aspect ratios).

